{
  "slug": "artist:hixxy",
  "name": "Hixxy",
  "editorial_article": "Born Ian Hicks in 1975, this Portsmouth-based DJ rose to prominence in the UK happy hardcore scene after he and DJ Sharkey released the 1995 track Toy Town on React Music. The track featured a mix of scruffy breaks and sugar-sweet vocals that critics identified as a turning point in rave history. Hixxy gained further reach as a foundational contributor to the Bonkers compilation series, which spawned 19 volumes and helped define the commercial trajectory of the genre. By 2004, his evolution into mainstream trance elements caught the attention of BBC Radio 1 DJ John Peel, who invited him for a guest mix later released as an official album. Alongside collaborators like Darren Styles and Mark Breeze, Hixxy initiated the Clubland X-Treme Hardcore compilation series in 2005, which yielded multiple gold-certified releases in the UK. He continues to perform at events like the Bang Face Weekender, often reuniting with long-time stage partner DJ Dougal.",
